# 🥉 Trace Labs OSINT Search Party

This isn't a replacement for a professional certification.

But it can be excellent evidence of **hands-on OSINT practice**.

Trace Labs runs OSINT Search Party CTFs around missing-person investigations and provides participation badges; its documentation also contains challenges, training and CTF write-ups. ([Trace Labs Docs][8])

[Trace Labs training documentation](https://docs.tracelabs.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### Priority

**★★★★★ for practice**

---

# 🔥 IntelTechniques OSIP

This is much more advanced.

Current IntelTechniques training is **$699/year**, and the optional OSIP assessment costs another **$300**. Completing its training is a prerequisite for the assessment. ([IntelTechniques][9])

The assessment is interesting because you're expected to take an investigation **from mission briefing to completed professional case file/report**. ([IntelTechniques][10])

### Priority

**★★★★☆ — after real experience**

Don't rush this in your first 60 days.

---

# 🏆 GIAC GOSI

**GIAC Open Source Intelligence — GOSI**

This is the premium track.

It covers:

* OSINT methodology
* Collection
* Analysis
* Reporting
* Dark-web intelligence
* OPSEC

The current exam has **75 questions, 2 hours, 69% passing score**. ([GIAC Certifications][11])

Its associated SANS SEC497 course currently has **36 hours and 29 labs**. Current US event pricing can be around **$8,780 for training + roughly $999 certification**, so it makes far more sense when an employer sponsors it. ([SANS Institute][2])

### Priority

**★★★★★ reputation / ★☆☆☆☆ beginner affordability**

Don't make this your first purchase.

